{"nodes": [{"id": "packages_db_readme", "label": "@missed-lead/db README", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "1-78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_customers", "label": "customers table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "17", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The tenant; 1:1 with an auth.users row today."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_lead_sources", "label": "lead_sources table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "18", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A webhook URL, forwarding address, or CSV upload. Carries webhook_token plus webhook_token_previous for rotation overlap, and a unique inbound_address."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_leads", "label": "leads table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The lead itself: surrogate uuid PK, email/phone plus their normalized forms, lead_status enum, estimated_value in integer cents, indexed on (customer_id, created_at desc) and (customer_id, status)."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_lead_identities", "label": "lead_identities table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "20", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Contact points a lead is reachable at \u2014 the merge key. unique(customer_id, kind, value_normalized) is what lets the same human arriving through two channels collapse onto one lead."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_lead_events", "label": "lead_events table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "21", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ingest audit trail plus idempotency key: unique(customer_id, dedupe_key). Also holds raw_payload and the per-ingest parse_errors/parse_warnings, which are diagnostics of a delivery rather than attributes of a lead."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_detection_settings", "label": "detection_settings table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "22", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-tenant thresholds feeding detectLeaks; defaults mirror the existing module constants exactly so behaviour is unchanged until a customer edits them."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_push_tokens", "label": "push_tokens table", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "23", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Devices to notify, empty until the notification phase \u2014 created now so that phase needs no tenancy migration. last_seen_at tracks token rot."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_rls_grants_nothing", "label": "RLS grants nothing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "27-30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Policies filter WITHIN privileges a role already holds. Drizzle emits CREATE POLICY but never GRANT, so a new table without an explicit grant makes every query return error 42501. If you add a table, add its grants in the same migration."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_0002_grants_sql", "label": "0002_grants.sql", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_with_ingest_scope", "label": "withIngestScope(db, customerId, fn)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "32-37", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sets a transaction-local app.customer_id and switches to ingest_role. Needs a real transaction, so a stateless HTTP driver will not work."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_ingest_role", "label": "ingest_role (NOBYPASSRLS)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "32-37", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ingest is unauthenticated \u2014 a form tool POSTs to a secret URL, so there is no auth.uid() and the authenticated policies cannot apply. ingest_role is NOBYPASSRLS so a bug cannot write across tenants, and an unset scope fails closed."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_two_dedupe_mechanisms", "label": "Two dedupe mechanisms, for two different problems", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "39-49", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Retried delivery \u2192 lead_events.dedupe_key \u2192 recordLeadEvent() no-ops. Same person via two channels \u2192 lead_identities \u2192 upsertLead() merges onto the existing lead. The second is the guard against double-counted revenue: if it breaks the product reports a wrong number rather than an obvious error, so its tests are worth keeping strict."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_record_lead_event", "label": "recordLeadEvent()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No-ops when a duplicate dedupe_key arrives, making retried deliveries idempotent."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_upsert_lead", "label": "upsertLead()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "43-45", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Matches on any normalized identity and merges onto the existing lead instead of inserting a second one."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_merge_lead_fields", "label": "mergeLeadFields \u2014 pure merge function", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "58", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pure, database-free, exercised by merge.test.ts. Rules: never null out a known value (an incoming null or absent field is ignored); a known value is never overwritten by a different one for name/phone/email/notes; timestamps only advance, never move backwards; terminal statuses never regress to an earlier status; estimated_value only rises, never falls. Returns {} when there is nothing to change."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_merge_test", "label": "merge.test.ts (pure, needs no database)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "58", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_prove_isolation", "label": "test:prove-isolation / prove-isolation.sh", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "55-63", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Loosens leads_tenant_isolation to using (true), asserts the suite goes red, then restores it. Always run it after touching policies or grants: a green isolation test that cannot detect a breach is false confidence."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_leads_tenant_isolation_policy", "label": "leads_tenant_isolation policy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "60-61", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_anon_key_client_assertions", "label": "Isolation assertions go through an anon-key client carrying a user JWT", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "65-67", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A service-role client bypasses RLS and would make the suite pass while proving nothing."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_custom_migration", "label": "drizzle-kit generate --custom", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "71-78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Use --custom for raw SQL (roles, grants) rather than hand-writing a file, because it registers the journal entry that migrate reads."}, {"id": "packages_db_readme_database_url_direct", "label": "Migrations run against DATABASE_URL_DIRECT", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "77-78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DDL needs session state a transaction pooler will not hold."}], "edges": [{"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_two_dedupe_keys", "target": "packages_db_readme_two_dedupe_mechanisms", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "39-49", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_ingest_role", "target": "packages_db_readme_ingest_role", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "32-37", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_tenant_isolation_policy", "target": "packages_db_readme_leads_tenant_isolation_policy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "packages/db/README.md", "source_location": "60-61", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_negative_control", "tar